  "description": "What Grafana's standard **Value mappings** option does on a relations panel, one use case per panel. Three things actually happen: mapped text replaces a mark's number in the tooltip row and in the node value label; a mapping carrying a `color` recolours the mark; and a mapping is per *field*, so it targets one node or one edge rather than the panel. None of it is implemented by the plugin \u2014 it all arrives through `field.display`, the display processor `applyFieldOverrides` already built. The fifth panel is the counter-example: a null-matching mapping that fires and is still never shown, which is why the \"No value\" standard option is unregistered for this family.",
  "refresh": "",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": ["echarts", "relations", "standard-options", "value-mappings"],
