    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "Value \u2192 text on a node stat",
      "description": "**A `ValueToText` mapping reaches both places a node stat is shown.** `1`/`2`/`3` become `Healthy`/`Degraded`/`Down`, in the label under each node name **and** in the tooltip's value row.\n\nNothing in the plugin implements this: a mark's value is formatted by its own field's display processor (`getValueFormatter` \u2192 `field.display`), which `applyFieldOverrides` already built with the mappings applied. So a mapping targets **one mark** \u2014 set it as a `byName` override and a single node reads `Healthy` while its neighbours stay numeric.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource",
        "uid": "trlxrdZVk"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "Healthy",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "2": {
                  "text": "Degraded",
                  "index": 1
                },
                "3": {
                  "text": "Down",
                  "index": 2
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single"
        },
        "seriesType": "graph",
        "relationsLayout": "circular",
        "relationsShowNodeValues": true
      },
      "targets": [
