    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "Mapping a colour, not just text",
      "description": "**The undocumented half: a mapping's `color` colours the mark.**\n\nSame three mappings as the panel to the left, each now carrying a colour. `colorOf` reads `field.display(value).color`, and `DisplayProcessor` sets that from the matched mapping \u2014 so the node symbols turn green/orange/red even though the colour scheme is still `palette-classic`.\n\nThis is the use case that makes value mappings worth having here: a status field becomes a topology coloured by status, with no thresholds and no per-node overrides.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource",
        "uid": "trlxrdZVk"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "Healthy",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "2": {
                  "text": "Degraded",
                  "color": "orange",
                  "index": 1
                },
                "3": {
